 "limitations": [
  "One pixel is an illustration, not a sample: it was chosen among the candidates of a rule, or by judgment where the selection record says so (the record gives their number and its rank), and it says nothing about other pixels.",
  "The class spectra come from one clear day, the cells of each class inside this pixel, and one 2021 land cover map. They are not typical spectra of the classes, and a 10 m cell at the edge of a class mixes surfaces.",
  "The mix model assumes the pixel's reflectance is the share-weighted sum of its class medians. It ignores shadow, slope and variation inside a class, so its NDVI is modelled, not measured, and it differs from the measured pixel NDVI by the amount stored.",
  "NDVI measures how green the ground looks from above, not forage, palatability or species; the main classes here are grassland and tree cover, which may include open woodland and savanna.",
  "The series is the pixel's own greenness for the window of the selection record, not adjusted for rainfall. Its trend is a descriptive Theil-Sen slope with Sen's 95% interval, and no p-value or false discovery rate class is stored for one pixel (SCI-52).",
  "Terra's overpass has drifted earlier since 2020, from 10:30 to about 9:06 mean local time by December 2025 (NASA), so later seasons are seen with a lower sun and longer shadows in mountain terrain, which may shift NDVI without any change on the ground.",
  "The catchment is a hydrological analysis extent, not a pasture, grazing lease or management boundary.",
  "The monthly Sentinel-2 median NDVI and its date count shown for each cell were built for this pixel's display window alone, by the same rules as the catchment-wide monthly bundle of the first place (scene classes 4 and 5, DN / 10000, same-date tiles merged, median over dates); there is no catchment-wide Sentinel-2 monthly bundle for this place. The true colour is display only."
